# =============================================================================
# Procfile.dev  (Docker-free local dev — run all services with one command)
# =============================================================================
# A Procfile lists named processes as "name: command". Run them together with
# honcho (the Python foreman clone, in the dev dependency group), e.g.:
#     honcho -f Procfile.dev start
# honcho launches all three uvicorn servers as local processes, prefixes and
# interleaves their logs, and shuts them all down together on Ctrl-C. This is
# the lightweight alternative to docker-compose for day-to-day development.
#
# Notes vs. docker-compose:
#   - Ports match the compose setup (content 8001, ai 8002, web 8000) so the
#     default localhost URLs in .env.example just work.
#   - `--reload` makes uvicorn hot-restart on source edits (dev only; never in
#     the containers, whose CMD omits it).
#   - No SERVICE_TOKEN/CONTENT_URL/etc. are set here; they come from your `.env`
#     (or the pydantic-settings defaults), unlike compose which sets them inline.

# content service: owns project data, listens on 8001.
content: uv run uvicorn content_service.main:app --port 8001 --reload
# ai service: chat + tool-use loop (calls content), listens on 8002.
ai: uv run uvicorn ai_service.main:app --port 8002 --reload
# web BFF: orchestrates content + ai, serves the site on 8000.
web: uv run uvicorn web_service.main:app --port 8000 --reload
